        "content": "<p>dsecurity49 opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14238\">PR #14238</a> from <code>dsecurity49:fix-aarch64-scalar-size-f16-f128</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>In <code>cranelift/codegen/src/isa/aarch64/inst.isle</code>, <code>scalar_size</code> is declared as a total term:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"isle\"><pre><span></span><code>(decl scalar_size (Type) ScalarSize)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It defined rules for integer types (<code>I8</code>..<code>I128</code>) and <code>F32</code> / <code>F64</code>, but omitted <code>F16</code> and <code>F128</code>.</p>\n<p>When ISLE lowering rules (such as <code>fma.f16</code>) passed an <code>F16</code> or <code>F128</code> type to <code>scalar_size</code>, the Cranelift compiler panicked with an internal ISLE error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">worker</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">panicked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">isle_aarch64</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">3755</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">internal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">entered</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unreachable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">code</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">no</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matched</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">scalar_size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">isa</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">aarch64</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1587</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">should</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partial</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Fix</h2>\n<p>Add the missing ISLE rules for <code>F16</code> and <code>F128</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"isle\"><pre><span></span><code>(rule (scalar_size $F16) (ScalarSize.Size16))\n(rule (scalar_size $F128) (ScalarSize.Size128))\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Testing</h2>\n<p>Added <code>cranelift/filetests/filetests/isa/aarch64/fma-f16.clif</code> and verified natively on AArch64 hardware:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">clif</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">util</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">cranelift</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">filetests</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">filetests</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">isa</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">aarch64</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">fma</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">f16</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">clif</span>\n<span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tests</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
