    {
        "content": "<p>dsecurity49 edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14238\">PR #14238</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Add missing <code>F16</code> and <code>F128</code> rules to <code>scalar_size</code> in <code>inst.isle</code>, as well as their corresponding models in <code>prelude.isle</code>.</p>\n<p>Without these, rules that pass <code>f16</code> or <code>f128</code> types to <code>scalar_size</code> (like <code>fma.f16</code>) trigger an ISLE panic because <code>scalar_size</code> is a total term.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620293256,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788178469
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14238#discussion_r3898287599\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We usually have compile-tests with the <code>precise-output</code> flag to show (and lock down) the actual compilation output. Could you include that here? And could you add something for <code>f128</code> as well if aarch64 has lowerings for it (I don't remember if it does)?</p>\n</blockquote>",
