    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> dsecurity49 submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14238#pullrequestreview-5074161311\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 620529090,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788238796
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> dsecurity49 created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14238#discussion_r3900909214\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>After checking further, keeping the F128 rule would be misleading,f128 arithmetic hits unexpected scalar FP operand size (size128)deeper in the backend anyway, so the scalar_size rule for it is effectively dead code. I've removed it and the corresponding model from prelude.isle, keeping only the F16 fix.</p>\n</blockquote>",
